{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJThNVVvU8SsLUmL2Sk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011qnBgGPZuzX5DndL5efeb5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-LuNyBX/memory/api-error-response-convention.md","content":"---\nname: api-error-response-convention\ndescription: Agreed API error body format with the mobile team: { \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\" } }, UPPER_SNAKE_CASE codes\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nEvery error response body must be `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`. The `code` is upper case with underscores, e.g. `INVOICE_NOT_FOUND`.\n\n**Why:** Agreed with the mobile team. The mobile app switches on `code` and shows `message` to the user as-is, so codes are a stable contract and messages must be user-presentable.\n\n**How to apply:** Use this format for any new or changed error response. The plain-text errors in `lib/routes.js` predate the convention and will be migrated separately, so don't copy their style, and don't migrate them unless asked. Don't rename existing codes casually, since the mobile app depends on them.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9727,"cache_read_input_tokens":11962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9727,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7db8a3b-ede2-4adc-83de-9e767e73ab9a","uuid":"89319d85-d69e-4293-b765-4bd7b569c0d4","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:27:38.115Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJThGY83ChCUmhVz6KR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011qnBgGPZuzX5DndL5efeb5":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-LuNyBX/memory/api-error-response-convention.md","content":"---\nname: api-error-response-convention\ndescription: Agreed API error body format with the mobile team: { \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\" } }, UPPER_SNAKE_CASE codes\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nEvery error response body must be `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`. The `code` is upper case with underscores, e.g. `INVOICE_NOT_FOUND`.\n\n**Why:** Agreed with the mobile team. The mobile app switches on `code` and shows `message` to the user as-is, so codes are a stable contract and messages must be user-presentable.\n\n**How to apply:** Use this format for any new or changed error response. The plain-text errors in `lib/routes.js` predate the convention and will be migrated separately, so don't copy their style, and don't migrate them unless asked. Don't rename existing codes casually, since the mobile app depends on them.\n"}}}
